  "agent": "Sotheby's International Realty - San Francisco Brokerage",
  "text": "The Art of Private Living. Behind a deliberately understated facade lies a home of rare beauty, created for those who treasure privacy and live well. Offering approximately 3,790 square feet on an oversized lot, this fully renovated residence features four bedrooms, three and a half baths, an office, and a pentroom. Awash in natural light, it pairs soaring ceilings, walls of glass, and gleaming hardwood floors with a generous garden and multiple decks for effortless indoor-outdoor living. Enter through a private courtyard into a gracious foyer with a spacious walk-in coat closet. One floor up, the expansive main level flows seamlessly through the living room, office area, dining area, kitchen, and family room, all bathed in light. The showstopping gourmet kitchen is the heart of the home, anchored by a long center island made for casual meals and lively gatherings. The family room features a dramatic wall of glass and French doors that open to a deck, which steps down to the large garden, where a gas fire pit sets the scene for cozy evenings under the stars. A private guest suite and an elegant powder room complete this level. Upstairs, the light-filled primary suite is a true retreat, overlooking the garden greenery below. It offers a large walk-in closet and a spa-inspired bath featuring double sinks, an oversized shower, and a deep soaking tub. This level also includes two additional bedrooms, a spacious full bath, and a laundry room. The pentroom delivers the wow. Decks on both sides and sweeping open-air space make this the natural place to move the party after dinner below, for cocktails, conversation, and nights that linger. A deep two-car garage with EV charging and abundant storage adds everyday ease. Step outside and enjoy the vibrant neighborhood, home to some of the city's most celebrated restaurants: dinner and a movie in the courtyard at Foreign Cinema, a legendary wine list at Heirloom Cafe, and handmade pasta at Flour + Water.",
