  "agent": "Compass",
  "text": "346 Lexington puts the best of San Francisco right outside your door. Set on a coveted tree-lined Liberty Hill street, this top-floor Italianate Victorian condo pairs period character with thoughtful updates. Tall Pella windows and French doors fill the home with natural light, while a wonderful cross-breeze flows from front to back. Hardwood floors and original details give the home its soul, while the refreshed kitchen, remodeled bath, cement tile, and new lighting bring it into the present. The two-bedroom, one-bath layout makes room for a living room, kitchen, dedicated dining room or office, and in-unit laundry. Wake up to a Giant Bird of Paradise outside your bedroom window, then step onto the rear balcony for a quiet moment of your own. And when you're ready to head out, the Mission is right there: restaurants, live music, bars, shops, and galleries in every direction. J-Church and BART are nearby, too. A classic San Francisco home with room to work, unwind, and make the city yours.",
